I managed to enchant my starting long sword (to be Excalibur)
to +5 at a fairly early stage of the game. I rode a little at first, and only
used lance to potentially dangerous foes like floating eyes.
I found armor like elven mithril coat, boots, helm and a shield.
The elves make great stuff, I have to admit.

Minetown priest was co-aligned. I lost Bill early on... and found
luckstone from the mine's end. The shops contained mildly
interesting items. 

>From Sokoban I got a BoH. I didn't dare go into Ludios, because
I had no MR or reflection. On the levels below Ludios and Quest,
my items would burn and all kinds of bolt attacks would hit me.
To my salvation, perhaps, I decided to do the Quest anyway. I had
a cunning plan, after all...

I tamed a horse with an apple. I had gotten teleport control, so I 
got teleportitis too. I had realized that Ixoth's lair was a teleport-zone,
so I wrote Elbereth on the staircase up, teleported to Ixoth and angered
him. Then I teleported to the staircase, riding Minerva the horse the
whole time. Then I jousted Ixoth to death. Great, I got the Magic Mirror
of Merlin! 

Shortly after the quest I took time to identify my stuff. Gosh, I had two
lamps the whole time, and the other one was a blessed magic lamp!
I cashed it for a SDSM. 

Now Ludios was easy. I polypiled there a lot, practiced spellcasting and
dipped for water. I had at least 1 spare item for every useful item, ie.
I had two unenchanted lances lying around in Ludios. I also got
lucky polying unicorn horns into magic markers.
At one point, I alchemized and produced about 25 potions of
Full Healing at one session...

At one point I got about 25 tins of spinach! Well, no more
worries about strenght. I tamed my first silver dragon, Silver at Ludios.
Before Castle, though, it turned into a statue because a cockatrice
bit it.

I descended and made my way to the Castle. I read 2 scrolls of earth, filled
the moat, destroyed the drawbridge,(killing ie. an ogre) and pushed
some boulders on the trapdoors so I could visit the store rooms.
I upgraded my AK by wishing. Now the rest of the game would be easy.
I got a +Stone to Flesh. I revived the statue of Silver, and descended.

But Gehennom can change a lot of things. The demons were of no serious
trouble, but a chameleon corpse turned Silver into a gold golem. Great...
Deep in Gehennom, a master mind flayer nibbled my brain, and I had to
map some of the levels again. 

Disenchanters mostly disenchanted my weapons. When my +6 lance
went to +5, it was nice. When my silver saber or Excalibur went from
+7 to +6, it wasn't. However, my [CoMR went from +4 to +3, and that
was nice.

I did some nurse-dancing at the Camelot Castle. Wow, I got well over 100
more hp. Why I hadn't done this more often?

I tamed another silver dragon, Saint. I think I got it too from Fort Ludios, where
I had locked it. I let Saint eat some wraith corpses, and I also let it kill many
monsters. It grew quite nicely, and it had about 200 hp. 

Because I wanted to practice jousting, I didn't want to shatter my lance, so I tried
to keep my luck high at all times. I had two +7 lances and two +0 in Ludios.
I threw precious gems to white unicorns and sacrificed after every water
prayer I could. 

I also tried to follow the knight conduct. This turned to be
a bit tricky, because Elbereth makes monsters scared.
Too many times I relied on a jousting attack to succeed against mind flayers,
and the results were not nice. 

When I acquired a tin whistle, I could wake up sleeping monsters.
Leprechauns I awakened by throwing gold at them.
By wielding a silver saber with a lance provided some good results:
if a jousting attack was unsuccesful, the lance would still hit, and so would
the saber. If the monster was against a wall and a jousting attack would
succeed, so would the silver saber slash.

Keeping Saint alive proved to be a tough job in the end,
but it was worth it. I revived Saint many times with a wand of /oUT. 
How does Knight's #turn -command work, anyway? 

Well, the Amulet run was definately interesting. The Wizard just kept reappearing,
and he appeared in the Moloch's sanctum. I read the Book near the
graveyard and tamed the many of undead while confused.

Then I attacked the Wizard(s) and the High Priestess of Moloch. Eventually
I got the Amulet and up I went... and down due to the mysterious force.
Lots of monsters kept appearing, Saint kept dying (I healed and revived it a lot), 
mmfs ate my brain... grr. I had to use my second magic lamp to wish for 2
blessed scrolls of enchant weapon, because I couldn't write any.
And the stupid dragon would eat every time I needed
to go up the stairs. But eventually I made it.

I didn't want to use conflict on the Planes...
Earth was easy, Air took some time due air elementals
(luckily I had lots of /oTeles) and Fire was dangerous for Saint.
Water was quickly over.

I had to search through the Astral Plane. Right temple: Famine.
It was easy jousting him to death. Darn, wrong temple...
Middle temple: Pestilence! Ick, I had to cast cure sickness repeatedly
in the middle of fighting against him. 
Left altar: Death was a wimp this time, and was easily jousted
to death. I made it to the high temple of Lugh, offered the Amulet and...

